everything I expected and more,

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:49.469 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, I come to Newsmax
from that perspective,

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.871
I had actually kind
of had grown jaded

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:97% position:3%
with the television business
and local news business,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.877
because there had been a lot
of corporate consolidation

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:01.614 align:start size:97% position:3%
and there was less
autonomy at the local level

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.217
for reporters like myself

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.653 align:start size:84% position:16%
and anchors to
pursue stories that

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
I felt like were really
important to our audience.

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.625
There were a lot of mandates
from the corporate offices

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you know edicts
from on high,

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.162
and we're gonna focus on this

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.697 align:start size:63% position:38%
and
(sighs)

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.733
I think that's problematic
with our country right now

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
where you have a
lot less local news,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:84% position:16%
a lot less investment
in local news,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you have less
coverage of the places

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:34.047
where the rubber really meets
the road in our democracy.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's in your County
Commission meetings

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:39.052
your school board meetings,
your city council meetings

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.087
and we're seeing this
right now I think Dave

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:44.824
with the vaccine rollout or
you had a very successful

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.894
operation Warp Speed
on the federal level,

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.063
and then when those resources,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.032
whether it's vaccines
or money from FEMA,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.335
when they get down
on the local level,

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:56.836
you really see a breakdown

00:03:56.836 --> 00:04:01.040 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the ability to execute
these types of national plans.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
And here I am, you
know I worked so hard,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.813
this was always kind of my goal

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.849
to get to a place where I
had a national audience,

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.385
but now that we're
here and you see the,

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.886
you know the pandemic response

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:17.924
and the disparate response
from California and New York

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.226
versus Florida and
how it's affecting

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.694
the mental health of people,

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:25.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you think about other
things too, in Georgia

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.567
or other states where you
had a complete breakdown

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.636 align:start size:84% position:16%
of confidence in
the election system,

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.070
you realize that this is really

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.172
where our focus needs to be now

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:36.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so as we kind of
reposition ourselves here,

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.978
looking ahead to the
Biden administration,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:84% position:16%
and of course keeping
an eye on that,

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:44.417 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have got to also
do a better job

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:48.254 align:start size:84% position:16%
of introducing America
to state houses

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:50.690
and what's going
on at a local level

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.125
so that we can understand

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.626
what's not working
in this country.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.428
I mean, this is still a
federalist system we have

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we're all fighting
to protect that,

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:00.300 align:start position:0%
and we still have, fortunately,
we still have this kind of

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.337
laboratory of ideas when it
comes to different policies

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:06.739 align:start size:97% position:3%
and prescriptions for problems
we have in this country.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:09.342
And again, we're seeing that
with this with this pandemic

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:11.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
and completely different
approaches from Cuomo

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.646
and Gavin Newsome
versus Ron DeSantis

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.515 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we know sometimes
that doesn't work

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.517
and now, I'm sure
a lot of people

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:18.751
are looking at the Florida model

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.387 align:start size:84% position:16%
and say, maybe Florida
man isn't so crazy.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that's kind of a
winding narrative here

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:26.059
but you know why I'm
attracted to you Dave

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:27.593
and why I had you on our show

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.429 align:start size:84% position:16%
is because this
idea of free thought

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.697
and that's why I'm
here at Newsmax now

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:33.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
because this provides
me the platform

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.600
to do the things I couldn't do

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.204
as a traditional quote
unquote news anchor.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.172
- It's interesting,

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:41.140
I asked you John Bachman 101

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.408
a little bit about your history,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.644
we talked about COVID
response, federalism,

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:47.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
government, television,
the whole thing,

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:51.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
so before we go any further,
you work for Newsmax.

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.186
- Yes.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.521
- Isn't that some
sort of far right

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.291
crazy extremist network,

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.225
John?

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.059
- That's what they tell me.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.294
You know,

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:02.762 align:start size:97% position:3%
the funny thing is too Dave
(chuckles)

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:05.264 align:start size:97% position:3%
is it's all that, of course
in some people's minds,

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:08.267 align:start size:84% position:16%
then at the same
time, I'm a traitor,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.802
for saying all the
way back in December

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:12.872
and just trying to tell the
audience that yes, you know

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:16.776
the bar is very high for Joe
Biden not to become president.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:19.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think we talked about
this that at a certain point

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.748 align:start position:0%
it was like a space shuttle
that had launched into the sky,

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:24.183 align:start size:88% position:13%
and if it didn't make
it into space into orbit

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.451
it was gonna be some sort of

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.253
catastrophic explosion
that would prevent it,

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.488
and it never happened,

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:29.756
I mean, we're here now.

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:31.391
And it, you know, I think,

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.960
you know, when you're taking
flack from the extreme right

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.095 align:start size:84% position:16%
as we are, when people
call me a traitor

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.030
for calling Joe Biden
the president elect

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.432
or from the far left, because

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.834
we just wanna do
something simple

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.170
as carry the president of
the United States speech,

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
which I think we were the
only major network to do that

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:48.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
this week when the president
was down at the border,

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.576 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, he's still the
president of the United States

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:52.211
and his words still matter

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.781
and nobody really
wants to do that.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:59.652
What we try to do is kind
of chart a different path

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.087
and provide information

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
that wasn't being provided
for a lot of people

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:06.092
and that somehow Dave has
become a radical idea.

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:09.295
- Do you find it sort of
tough to be a news anchor

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:13.766
in a time when not only is
there cable news obviously

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:15.368
and sort of the
dying dinosaur of

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:18.805 align:start size:84% position:16%
the big three cable
news channels,

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:19.906
but now there's a whole bunch

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:21.374
of other channels like Newsmax,

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:23.810 align:start size:84% position:16%
then there's like
the gazillion people

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.945
on YouTube and podcasts
and everywhere else,

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
but finding a niche that
actually makes sense

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:31.150
that's still true to who you are

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.720 align:start size:97% position:3%
is sort of tough just business
wise and everything else.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yes, I do, I think it
is tough in some respects.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.758
I mean, I think,

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:40.193 align:start size:81% position:19%
you know there are
very few places

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:42.728 align:start size:88% position:13%
that can provide me
this type of opportunity

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.764 align:start size:97% position:3%
there are other great people
we have that work for us.

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.499
I mean, you know
Chris Roddy our CEO

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.402
really is a believer in
the idea of a big tent

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:52.505 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you know, individuality
and you know the

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:57.510
competition of ideas and
that's what he promotes

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.947
and it was kind of kind of a
random way that he and I met,

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:03.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
I talked about my background
as a TV news reporter,

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:06.118 align:start size:88% position:13%
I remember one day
specifically I woke up,

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
was reading the newspaper,
the Palm Beach Post

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:09.622
and I read it a little blurb,

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:10.957
there was a great
political reporter

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.492 align:start size:84% position:16%
who no longer works
in local news.

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:13.626
He's gone on to do other things,

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:15.094
his name is George Bennett.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:16.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
He wrote about the
fact that Sarah Pailin

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:19.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
was going to a place
called Newsmax to visit,

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:23.503
this was after the 2008
presidential election,

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:25.304
she was obviously
a lightning rod

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.507
and I wanted to go
meet Sarah Pailin.

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.076
I was fascinated by her story,

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:32.612
her appeal to conservatives.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:34.013
And so I showed up at Newsmax,

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.548
not knowing much about Newsmax

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:37.083
and I worked the parking lot,

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:39.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
met some of the people who
showed up to meet Sarah Pailin

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:41.320
and asked them why they
were interested in her

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.289
and they liked her
outsider philosophy.

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:45.258
And you know, at that same time

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:47.727
that's when I met Chris
ruddy, the CEO of Newsmax

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:49.795
and he and I struck
up a conversation,

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.797 align:start size:84% position:16%
he and I talked
about a lot of things

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:53.266
I had expressed at that point,

00:08:53.266 --> 00:08:56.969
kind of my disillusionment
with the local news business,

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:58.304
and he gave me his business card

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.006
and said, hey, let's
go to lunch sometime.

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:02.408 line:0%
And at that point
I was interested in

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:04.277 line:0%
what he had to say
about the business

00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:06.779 line:0%
and long story short,
that was 10 years ago

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:08.648 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he had mentioned
at that lunch

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:11.150
the idea of starting
a cable news network

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.253
because he felt like there
was a vast portion of America

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.088
that even with Fox News

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.858
and other conservative outlets
that were not being reached.

00:09:18.858 --> 00:09:21.694 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so here we are
all these years later,

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:25.197 align:start size:88% position:13%
to have this opportunity
to be on your show,

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:29.902
to have this new audience
find us as an alternative

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:33.706 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a compliment to the
spectrum of conservative media

00:09:33.706 --> 00:09:36.208
that's available is
just really humbling.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.711
- Isn't that actually the
cool part that it's like

00:09:38.711 --> 00:09:41.380
