00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:00.506
still at the end of the day

00:14:00.506 --> 00:14:02.775
Dave is because we still have

00:14:02.775 --> 00:14:07.613
75 million people in this
country who appear sane,

00:14:07.613 --> 00:14:08.747
and you know which side

00:14:08.747 --> 00:14:09.415 align:start size:81% position:19%
(laughing)
I'm talking about,

00:14:09.415 --> 00:14:10.816
which voters.

00:14:10.816 --> 00:14:12.985 align:start position:0%
And again, I don't wanna
pretend like I'm a partisan here

00:14:12.985 --> 00:14:15.221
but when you look
at the comparison,

00:14:15.221 --> 00:14:16.589
it's a stark contrast and

00:14:17.823 --> 00:14:21.193
it's hard for me
to see how people

00:14:21.193 --> 00:14:22.428
went the other way sometimes.

00:14:22.428 --> 00:14:23.662
But again, that's
just my opinion,

00:14:23.662 --> 00:14:25.764 align:start size:84% position:16%
I guess I can say that
here in this forum.

00:14:25.764 --> 00:14:26.999
- Well, I'm curious though,

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:28.968
how do you balance that
on a day to day basis?

00:14:28.968 --> 00:14:30.202
Like when I do your show,

00:14:30.202 --> 00:14:32.504
it's pretty obvious to
me that you're a profe-,

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:34.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
like you are a
professional news man,

00:14:34.273 --> 00:14:36.876
do you consider yourself a
traditional journalist still?

00:14:36.876 --> 00:14:38.010 align:start size:81% position:19%
- No, I.
- Because you're,

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.478 align:start size:81% position:19%
it's obvious to me
(chuckles)

00:14:39.478 --> 00:14:41.013
that you have opinions and
you're not afraid to say them

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:42.681
but you are presenting news.

00:14:42.681 --> 00:14:45.050 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I think there's almost
an expectation now

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.586
from the audience not
to give your opinion

00:14:47.586 --> 00:14:49.622
but to be honest about
where you're coming from

00:14:49.622 --> 00:14:50.789
and I always talk about,

00:14:50.789 --> 00:14:52.258 align:start size:88% position:13%
this is not
necessarily my opinion,

00:14:52.258 --> 00:14:53.792
it's more or less
my perspective,

00:14:53.792 --> 00:14:56.962
giving people some insight
on where I'm coming from,

00:14:56.962 --> 00:14:58.230
you know, I grew up
in the deep South

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.299
but my parents are
from the Northeast,

00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:02.835
I almost, I consider myself a
first generation Southerner,

00:15:02.835 --> 00:15:05.804
even growing up in the
eighties and nineties

00:15:05.804 --> 00:15:08.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
Catholic in the Deep South
with Northern parents,

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:11.010 align:start size:97% position:3%
you'd have friends and they'd
be somewhat skeptical of,

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.445
are your carpet back,
what's going on here

00:15:13.445 --> 00:15:14.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
(laughing)
that type of thing.

00:15:14.613 --> 00:15:15.948
But again, you know,

00:15:15.948 --> 00:15:19.585
it's a diverse kind
of background to have

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:21.453
and a different way
of thinking at things

00:15:21.453 --> 00:15:24.290 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that's kind of just
always shaped my perspectives,

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:27.259
but people expect you to
kind of be honest with them

00:15:27.259 --> 00:15:29.261
where you're coming
from on these things.

00:15:29.261 --> 00:15:32.097
So I like to, say I
do two things here,

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:33.599
I'm gonna lay out
the facts for you

00:15:33.599 --> 00:15:35.668
and then I'm gonna tell you why

00:15:35.668 --> 00:15:37.903
specifically we chose
those set of facts

00:15:37.903 --> 00:15:40.172 align:start size:88% position:13%
because I have a limited
time for my show,

00:15:40.172 --> 00:15:42.608 align:start size:97% position:3%
so there are only so many
facts I can provide in there,

00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:45.911 align:start position:0%
and there are other news outlets
that focus on other facts.

00:15:45.911 --> 00:15:47.513
But these are the
facts that I think

00:15:47.513 --> 00:15:49.114
are the most important facts

00:15:49.114 --> 00:15:54.119
and those facts come based on
my history, where I grew up,

00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:56.088
what I believe, the
books I'm reading,

00:15:56.088 --> 00:15:57.356
the movies I'm watching

00:15:57.356 --> 00:15:58.791
and so I do try to
give the audience

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:00.292
insight on those things

00:16:00.292 --> 00:16:02.161
so they have kind of perspective

00:16:02.161 --> 00:16:03.996 align:start size:88% position:13%
on where my perspective
is coming from.

00:16:03.996 --> 00:16:06.899
And that, I talk
about this with my

00:16:06.899 --> 00:16:08.901 align:start size:88% position:13%
college journalism
professor all the time,

00:16:08.901 --> 00:16:11.236
David Hasinsky who used
to work at NBC news.

00:16:11.236 --> 00:16:13.105
He is admittedly a liberal

00:16:13.105 --> 00:16:15.274 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we argue about
politics all the time,

00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:17.543
but when it comes to the
practice of journalism,

00:16:17.543 --> 00:16:20.012
you know the rules are still
the same at the end of the day,

00:16:20.012 --> 00:16:21.513
trust your sources,

00:16:21.513 --> 00:16:24.116 align:start size:97% position:3%
give attribution to where
your information comes from,

00:16:24.116 --> 00:16:27.553
only choose sources that
are really trustworthy,

00:16:27.553 --> 00:16:29.922 align:start size:84% position:16%
tell people the truth,
what has happened,

00:16:29.922 --> 00:16:31.724
don't speculate too much

00:16:31.724 --> 00:16:34.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you stay within those
lines, it's not hard,

00:16:34.893 --> 00:16:35.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, it is hard,
it's difficult,

00:16:35.961 --> 00:16:37.930
but you can do both Dave.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.365
Give people the facts,

00:16:39.365 --> 00:16:41.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
be honest with them about
what's gonna happen,

00:16:41.367 --> 00:16:44.370
don't be afraid to call
him the president elect

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.871 align:start size:88% position:13%
when you know it's
gonna upset the audience

00:16:45.871 --> 00:16:48.474
because they might be upset
with you for a day or two

00:16:48.474 --> 00:16:51.076
and some people might
change the channel,

00:16:51.076 --> 00:16:52.911
but come January 20th,

00:16:52.911 --> 00:16:54.847
when I was honest with
the audience about what

00:16:54.847 --> 00:16:57.116 align:start size:97% position:3%
historically and
constitutionally the limits

00:16:57.116 --> 00:16:58.851 align:start size:84% position:16%
were for what actually
were gonna happen

00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:01.787
and that, Lynnwood
might not be right.

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:04.323
Long-term when you are right,

00:17:04.323 --> 00:17:06.725
they gravitate back towards you

00:17:06.725 --> 00:17:09.528
and they respect you for
being honest with them.

00:17:09.528 --> 00:17:12.164 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's, what you're able
to do with your audience,

00:17:12.164 --> 00:17:15.434
that is what I hope the
internet still provides,

00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:17.569 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're still on YouTube,
thank God for that.

00:17:17.569 --> 00:17:18.771
(laughing)
You know,

00:17:18.771 --> 00:17:20.039
and I think you're about

00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:22.508
to cross 1.5 million
followers on YouTube

00:17:22.508 --> 00:17:24.977
and YouTube would be nuts

00:17:24.977 --> 00:17:26.512 align:start size:84% position:16%
to take that platform
away from you

00:17:26.512 --> 00:17:28.414
because it would, you
would really upset

00:17:28.414 --> 00:17:31.150 align:start size:88% position:13%
or pissed-off I can
say, 1.5 million people.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:33.252
So, just like I have faith

00:17:33.252 --> 00:17:35.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the overall population
of the country,

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.189
I have faith in those
1.5 million people

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:38.690
who follow you on YouTube

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.393
and that they would pick up
the phone or do something

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:45.164
to force you to make sure that
you still have this platform.

00:17:45.164 --> 00:17:46.665
- Yeah, I hope you're right.

00:17:46.665 --> 00:17:49.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, I'm usually the
optimist on these interviews

00:17:49.902 --> 00:17:51.437 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I bring on people
who give me like,

00:17:51.437 --> 00:17:54.173 align:start size:97% position:3%
uh-oh, the whole world's going
to hell in a hand basket,

00:17:54.173 --> 00:17:56.408
but you're giving me the
optimist approach here.

00:17:56.408 --> 00:18:00.446 align:start position:0%
Do you think it's kind of funny
when like CNN, for example,

00:18:00.446 --> 00:18:01.780
like none of their anchors,

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:03.949
not that they ever
really do interviews,

00:18:03.949 --> 00:18:05.751
but that if they
did an interview,

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:07.986
I don't think that Wolf Blitzer

00:18:07.986 --> 00:18:12.291
or Don Lemon or Jake
Tapper or Brian Stelter

00:18:12.291 --> 00:18:15.461
or whatever the other made
up names are, pretend humans,

00:18:15.461 --> 00:18:17.663
I don't think that
they would admit

00:18:17.663 --> 00:18:20.065
the biases that you
just admit there.

00:18:20.065 --> 00:18:22.534 align:start position:0%
I think they would say no,
we're calling balls and strikes,

00:18:22.534 --> 00:18:23.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
(chuckles)
and it is what it is.

00:18:23.969 --> 00:18:26.071 align:start size:97% position:3%
Even Chris Cuomo, the
biggest clown in cable news,

00:18:26.071 --> 00:18:27.739
I think he would say, no,

00:18:27.739 --> 00:18:30.676
I'm not a Democrat
or a Republican, I'm
not left or right,

00:18:30.676 --> 00:18:31.910
I'm a newsman.

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.046
And it's that sort of
fraudulent nonsense

00:18:34.046 --> 00:18:35.314
that people can't stand.

00:18:35.314 --> 00:18:38.117
- My kind of test
for a news anchor,

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.852
I like to ask them how much time

00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:42.154 align:start size:88% position:13%
did you spend out in the
street as a reporter?

00:18:42.154 --> 00:18:43.388
How many doors did you knock?

00:18:43.388 --> 00:18:45.991
How many pairs of shoes
did you ruin stepping

00:18:45.991 --> 00:18:47.493
in things you shouldn't step in

00:18:47.493 --> 00:18:50.162
because you're a reporter

00:18:50.162 --> 00:18:52.231 align:start size:88% position:13%
and maybe you shouldn't
have been there?

00:18:52.231 --> 00:18:54.366
You know, I think like
that's kind of what's

00:18:54.366 --> 00:18:57.569
missing a lot of times
from our news anchors

00:18:57.569 --> 00:18:59.771
is they haven't talked
to enough regular people.

00:18:59.771 --> 00:19:02.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
The emphasis in
this business is on

00:19:02.241 --> 00:19:04.443
